<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: West of Ireland gets 600 more jobs, Bruton says.</title>
<headline>West of Ireland gets 600 more jobs, Bruton says.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enterprise and Employment Minister Richard Bruton announced on Wednesday a 20 million pound IDA-backed expansion proposal for jewellery maker Hans Andersen of Vienna.</p>
<p>&quot;This will create 200  new jobs in Ennis within four years increasing to 600 over the following years as the companycontinues to expand in its markets in Europe,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Andersen Ireland Ltd employes more than 300 people in Rathkeale producing &quot;Pierre Lange&quot; designer jewellery which I sold by direct marketing in Austria, Switzerland and Germany.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom + 661 3377</p>
</text>
